<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna calleeretpurge: an i386 struct-returning callee pops its hidden pointer.

    Built with clang -m32 -O1 -fomit-frame-pointer from
        struct S{int a,b,c;};
        __attribute__((noinline)) struct S f(int x){struct S s={x,x+1,x+2};return s;}
        __attribute__((noinline)) void h(int *p){ *p += 3; }
        int g(int y){int loc[4]; loc[0]=y; h(loc); struct S s=f(y); loc[1]=s.a; h(loc+1);
                     struct S t=f(loc[0]+s.c); h(loc+2); return loc[1]+t.b+loc[0]+loc[2];}

    f ends `ret $4` (i386 SysV: the callee pops the hidden return pointer), and g
    re-reserves the popped slot with `sub esp,4` after each call to f.
    x86gcc.cspec states extrapop=4 for every call, so with the option off every
    stack reference after a call to f drifts by 4: loc[0], loc[1] and loc[2] all
    read as `v2[0]`, s.c reads the wrong slot.  With the option on, f's decoded
    `ret $4` gives the call extrapop 8 and each loc[i] is its own slot.

    Stage: P4 callee prototype stack contract, option calleeretpurge off|on.
    Pass 1 (off) pins the bug, pass 2 (on, the default) pins the fix.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x8049000">

</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x8049000" name="f"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x8049020" name="h"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x8049030" name="g"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option calleeretpurge off</com>
  <com>lo fu g</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option calleeretpurge on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="CALLEERETPURGE #1: off, loc[1] and loc[2] collapse onto loc[0]" min="1" max="1">^  h\(v2\);$
^  f\(v3,v1\);$
^  v2\[0\] = v7;$
^  h\(v2\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEERETPURGE #2: on, loc[1] is its own slot, assigned from s.a" min="1" max="1">^  v4 = v3\[0\];$
^  h\(&amp;v4\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEERETPURGE #3: on, loc[2] is its own slot" min="1" max="1">^  h\(v6\);$
^  return v8 \+ v4 \+ v2 \+ v6\[0\];$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEERETPURGE #4: on, the second f gets loc[0] + s.c" min="1" max="1">^  f\(v5,v7 \+ v2\);$</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
